path: /artifact/the-serialized-node-is-a-node-id-h
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.416002+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:7e5c85c2-61c8-4061-9631-f3079d4cea25] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.416002+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:d0b815e4-5f91-4e65-83a2-04444a4d74ca] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.416002+00:00

The serialized node is a `[node:<id>]` header block, a blank line, then the body. The blank-line separator is load-bearing: edge-lines are inserted ABOVE it, so moving it silently changes what parses as body text. serialization.py's parser depends on this and so does every dump in git history.
