[node:921ae6cf-7f43-4322-ad65-aad10fa4734c]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/a-node-s-identity-is-its-store-generated
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.417068+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:7e5c85c2-61c8-4061-9631-f3079d4cea25] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.417068+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:d0b815e4-5f91-4e65-83a2-04444a4d74ca] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.417068+00:00

A node's identity is its store-generated uuid4; `path` is a display label, not an address. Two labels colliding on one slug is a readability wart, never a data bug (MT3-30). This is why capture never needs to negotiate a name, and why the same wording captured twice is two nodes.
---
