path: /artifact/snapshot-over-log-the-events-table-is-t
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.426761+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:4a3b8d2c-7c88-448b-8eab-b9726b9bcc2b] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.426761+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:7be44b5d-a570-4dd8-9963-64a56554321f] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.426761+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:b025e125-9a2b-4591-abf5-1982ea27e1a4] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.460116+00:00

Snapshot-over-log: the events table is the append-only source of truth, nodes.trust_weight is a materialized cache, and recompute_trust() is the explicit bridge between them. Recompute is LAZY — append_event never triggers it — which keeps the write path cheap and means a trust_weight column can legitimately lag its journal.
---
