[node:92a91b4e-34c0-490a-9979-6478b4f946d3]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/where-two-edges-of-different-types-join
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.432610+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.432610+00:00

Where two edges of different types join the same pair, the strongest policy weight wins and weights never stack. Found during testing: with stacking, adding a CONTRADICTS on top of an existing DEPENDS_ON would BOOST the target's structural pull — disagreement would have made a node more retrievable.
---
