[node:3ef8d9a0-397c-4c8d-b2d7-b377c3adc80f]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/ppr-row-normalizes-so-edge-policy-weigh
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.433396+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.433396+00:00

PPR row-normalizes, so edge-policy weights are relative per node, not absolute. A node whose only out-edge is CONTRADICTS (policy 0.25) still passes its full damped mass through it, because 0.25 normalizes to 1.0 when it is the only row entry. The policy table controls proportion between a node's edges, never the total it emits.
---
