[node:e08e5065-ba2a-4c0b-8883-6f528dff948e]
type: issue
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/seed-discovery-embeds-the-query-with-has
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.434870+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> ABOUT [node:3552de0d-0173-495a-b48e-7e62abcd9b46] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.434870+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.434870+00:00

Seed discovery embeds the query with hashed bag-of-words and compares it to facet-value bodies, so matching is LEXICAL: a query for 'billing' will not find a facet named 'invoicing'. The controlled facet vocabulary is the entire bridge between a query string and the graph, so this bounds recall for everything downstream. The Embedder port swap is the designed fix.
---
