[node:c07d53fe-a592-4be1-93a0-06c638016c30]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/tools-never-embed-judgment-skills-never
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.441476+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:71ed798c-7548-4e53-aa09-e072beeaea01] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.441476+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:b025e125-9a2b-4591-abf5-1982ea27e1a4] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.457825+00:00

Tools never embed judgment; skills never bypass tools. The MCP calls are deterministic operations, and the memory-* skills are the judgment layer that decides when to call them. Kept strictly (MT3-24): a tool that started deciding would make the surface untestable, and a skill that reached past the tools would escape the safety invariant.
---
