[node:fe0da020-4b5c-4520-bfef-f5551d72b360]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-gui-holds-exactly-the-operations-the
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:52:38.446308+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:775f9ad3-3734-4b06-8c0f-e1e899547b3f] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.446308+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:b025e125-9a2b-4591-abf5-1982ea27e1a4] @ 2026-09-06T11:52:38.458418+00:00

The GUI holds exactly the operations the agent surface forbids, and every human override is journaled as an event. That is what keeps a human override inside the audit trail instead of outside it: trust stays derived even when a person is the one deriving it, and the graph never has a state nobody can explain.
