The benchmark corpus is synthetic rather than mined from real project history. Nothing here asks an LLM to answer from context — the question is whether a deterministic algorithm ranks the right node first — so pretraining leakage is irrelevant and CONTROLLED VOCABULARY OVERLAP is what matters: you write the query and its gold node together and construct the hard cases deliberately.
