path: /artifact/a-degraded-mode-backlog-needs-a-detector
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:56:03.435186+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:71ed798c-7548-4e53-aa09-e072beeaea01] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.435186+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:9a146808-9866-484a-8ade-cd7279ff3d18] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.440259+00:00

A degraded-mode backlog needs a DETECTOR, not just a rule. The workflow said 'queue it and replay later'; nothing anywhere noticed that later never came, so one backlog sat unreplayed for a month while this project's own graph held two nodes. `memory_lifecycle.py backlogs` lists every backlog with no leading REPLAYED marker and the SessionStart hook runs it, so the queue is in front of the next agent before its first turn.
---
