[node:b0ceb87c-a326-4b1f-adbe-556c0df3635c]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-backlog-detector-opens-no-store-and
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:56:03.436445+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:71ed798c-7548-4e53-aa09-e072beeaea01] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.436445+00:00

The backlog detector opens NO store and answers a pure filesystem question. A backlog exists precisely because the store was unreachable, so a detector that needed the graph would be silent in exactly the situation it is built for. It also means the check costs nothing and cannot fail for the reason it is reporting on.
---
