[node:9c0052fa-bb07-41d5-9cb3-5511dd59f968]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/a-replayed-backlog-is-marked-with-a-line
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:56:03.437314+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:71ed798c-7548-4e53-aa09-e072beeaea01] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.437314+00:00

A replayed backlog is marked with a line starting `REPLAYED <date>`, and the marker must LEAD a line — 'not yet REPLAYED' still counts as outstanding. The marker is what makes a second replay refusable: capture is append-only with no idempotency key, so replaying a backlog twice mints duplicate nodes rather than reconciling with the first run.
---
