[node:b9029b10-010a-4a01-ae10-0fcbdd3753c9]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/backfilled-scopes-are-left-active-rather
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:56:03.438128+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:775f9ad3-3734-4b06-8c0f-e1e899547b3f] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.438128+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:b025e125-9a2b-4591-abf5-1982ea27e1a4] @ 2026-09-06T11:56:03.439699+00:00

Backfilled scopes are left ACTIVE rather than deactivated on capture. A completed change would normally be swept dormant, but only long-term and lifetime nodes survive a sweep, and those tiers are reachable only through human promotion — so sweeping a fresh backfill would bury every node before anyone had ruled on it. The scope stays live until the promotion gate has been walked, and closing it is the human's move.
---
