path: /artifact/the-test-suite-runs-in-ci-on-github-host
created_at: 2026-09-06T12:15:40.861134+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> CONTRADICTS [node:53a0fee4-bab0-4bb4-8f2c-760a10ba6599] @ 2026-09-06T12:15:40.861134+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c7bdc219-b9f2-4f03-8bf8-0588e4468eac] @ 2026-09-06T12:15:40.861134+00:00

The test suite runs in CI on GitHub-hosted ARM64 (`ubuntu-24.04-arm`), NOT on the org's Ampere self-hosted runner, which was the first choice. GitHub refuses to dispatch jobs from a PUBLIC repository to a self-hosted runner whose group has allows_public_repositories=false — verified empirically: the job queued indefinitely with the runner online, idle, and labelled correctly. Relaxing that policy would expose the maintainer's own hardware to arbitrary code from fork pull requests, which is not a trade worth making for a test suite. GitHub's ARM64 image keeps the architecture, is free for public repos, and runs the suite in about ten seconds.
---
