---
[node:f9d7105f-ac5e-401b-a8b1-552b9c513c5f]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-harness-measures-stage-1-and-stage-2
created_at: 2026-09-06T14:34:03.071072+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> CONTRADICTS [node:8d0e5438-0d42-4e7d-a3c4-d805b4af3572] @ 2026-09-06T14:34:03.071072+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T14:34:03.071072+00:00

The harness measures stage 1 and stage 2 separately and reports end-to-end as the headline, because an embedder swap can only move seed discovery and a weight retune can only move composition — a single blended number cannot say which happened. Stage 2 is isolated by seeding it with the MEMBERS OF THE GOLD FACET, which is what a perfect stage 1 would return, not with the gold node itself, which would make the measurement trivial.
---
[node:4b2ee944-4899-4ae9-a6b0-951804bc7cfc]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-goal-node-must-be-excluded-from-any
created_at: 2026-09-06T14:34:03.072363+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T14:34:03.072363+00:00

The goal node must be excluded from any measured ranking. recall_multi seeds the goal at weight 0.7, so it returns at rank 1 of every single query; leaving it in caps MRR at 0.5 no matter how good the ranker is and reports a perfect answer as mediocre. The goal is the question, not an answer to it.
---
[node:b2874ca8-76f7-419e-bb6e-99d4e5c1a653]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/a-benchmark-corpus-must-mint-node-ids-fr
created_at: 2026-09-06T14:34:03.073242+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T14:34:03.073242+00:00

A benchmark corpus must mint node ids from a seeded generator. Retrieval breaks score ties BY ID, so a corpus built with fresh uuid4s ranks tied nodes differently on every build and the numbers jitter for reasons unrelated to the code under test. Determinism of the algorithm is not enough — the corpus has to be rebuildable byte-identically or the benchmark measures its own randomness.
---
[node:c93d1e00-1032-4b07-980b-2f74fb27e405]
type: issue
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-ablation-matrix-is-not-yet-interpret
created_at: 2026-09-06T14:34:03.074005+00:00
needs_review: true
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 0.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T14:34:03.074005+00:00

The ablation matrix is not yet interpretable and must not be used to retune production weights. Every node in the corpus is created in one run with almost no journal events, so trust_weight and recency are nearly uniform; terms carrying no signal cannot help ranking and can only dilute the one term that does. That is why structure-only (alpha=1) currently beats the shipped blend by a wide margin — a property of the corpus, not evidence about alpha/beta/gamma. Making it interpretable needs seeded trust events and spread created_at values, with gold labels chosen so a low-trust node SHOULD rank below a high-trust one.
---
