[node:263ef4a7-9561-4ab5-a75d-d54114faa996]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/in-production-the-beta-term-is-only-the
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716011+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:7be44b5d-a570-4dd8-9963-64a56554321f] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716011+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716011+00:00

In production the beta term is ONLY the flag penalty, because trust_weight never varies. flag_contradicted journals a contradiction without folding it, recompute_trust is lazy, and its only production caller is a per-node button in the GUI — there is no batch. Every node in this repository's own graph sits at exactly 1.0, so beta*trust is a constant added to every candidate except flagged ones and cannot discriminate between two healthy nodes at any value of beta.
---
[node:69a3dad5-2933-4e33-81d8-5a8068ce3bf6]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/beta-is-also-the-ceiling-on-staleness-n
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716983+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:775f9ad3-3734-4b06-8c0f-e1e899547b3f] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716983+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.716983+00:00

beta is also the CEILING ON STALENESS, not just the trust weight. TrustTermPenalty computes hop*(alpha*retrieval + beta*trust*(1-p) + gamma*recency), so the review-flag penalty p reaches the score only through beta. Setting beta=0 does not merely ignore trust — it switches the staleness penalty off entirely, and a disputed node then ranks first. Anyone lowering beta to favour structure is quietly weakening staleness at the same time, and nothing in the code says so.
---
[node:4b42b552-831b-4add-9588-af381570eb19]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-static-model-embedder-model2vec-be
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.717872+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.717872+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:e08e5065-ba2a-4c0b-8883-6f528dff948e] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.717872+00:00

The static-model embedder (model2vec, behind the existing Embedder port) ships as an OPTIONAL extra and is never the default, opted into with MEMORY_EMBEDDER=static. A default that silently downloaded a model on first use would be exactly the out-of-band dependency docs/08_TRANSPORTS.md argues cannot be made transparent by documenting it better. Static embeddings were chosen over a sentence-transformer because they are a token lookup table: no torch, ~30MB, and deterministic by construction, so retrieval stays the pure function MT3-20 requires.
---
[node:1c8a0dee-5a96-4d04-ae8f-543270339e16]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-facet-collision-threshold-belongs-to
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.718735+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.718735+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:d0b815e4-5f91-4e65-83a2-04444a4d74ca] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.718735+00:00

The facet-collision threshold belongs to the EMBEDDER, not to the governance code (Embedder.suggest_threshold). It is a property of that embedder's similarity scale: hashed bag-of-words puts a genuine near-duplicate at 0.50 and an unrelated pair at 0.00, while the static model puts the same pairs at 0.41-0.75 and 0.00-0.19. Swapping the embedder while leaving the hardcoded 0.35 behind would silently switch facet-collision detection off and the controlled vocabulary would stop being controlled with nobody told. The static model's 0.30 was measured against those pairs, not guessed — an initial guess of 0.55 would have missed two of four real collisions.
---
[node:0ad01f9d-098d-45d8-bae1-39841825bb96]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/measured-result-of-the-embedder-swap-st
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.719500+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.719500+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:c93d1e00-1032-4b07-980b-2f74fb27e405] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.719500+00:00

Measured result of the embedder swap: stage-1 facet recall on paraphrase queries goes 0.00 -> 0.80 and end-to-end top-1 success does not move at all (0.67 both ways). What improves is the shape of the rest of the ranking — focus 0.87 -> 0.97, noise 0.32 -> 0.25 — because better seeds redistribute PPR mass among nodes the goal already reaches rather than reaching different ones. The obvious explanation, that goal_weight=0.7 caps the supplementary seeds, was TESTED AND REFUTED: lowering it to 0.5 and 0.3 leaves paraphrase success flat. So the swap is worth having if a caller reads past rank 1, which an agent consuming a recall bundle does, and is not worth a required model download for top-1 accuracy.
---
[node:a70015dd-a95e-499c-96e5-f7a6395024df]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/mrr-is-the-wrong-metric-for-a-query-whos
created_at: 2026-09-06T15:22:02.720369+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:ac7287ee-97a0-4725-9a12-1441b544f6a9] @ 2026-09-06T15:22:02.720369+00:00

MRR is the wrong metric for a query whose correct outcome is demotion. For the contradiction category the gold node is the FLAGGED one and TrustTermPenalty's documented job is to keep it reachable but not first — so MRR rewards precisely the failure, and a weighting that disables the penalty scores as an improvement. Benchmark queries carry an expected outcome (first / demoted) and are scored against it. The design had warned about this in words and the harness did it anyway on its first version.
---
